 Earlier n=8/M=3 read was "AMBIGUOUS/underpowered"; the M=5/n=19 run supersedes it as a clean powered null on the behavior half. Artifact `results/arc_incontext_pattern_proposal_ab.json` (substrate=aggregation over 19 per-game live-LLM checkpoints; adversarial_verify clean; verifier_is_oracle=False; solve_provenance=development_proxy).
 
+**LLM-as-TOOL-DRIVER / MCP loop over ARC subsystems (operator-asked 2026-06-28; AUDITED not-done-before, NOT YET BUILT):** the operator asked whether, instead of context-INJECTION, we have given the LLM an MCP/function-calling loop to actively INTERROGATE+DRIVE the live agent (env.step/state), the BFS frontier, any TRMs, and the generated game (world-model) code — i.e. the LLM holds the steering wheel and decides the next move from tool results. A 9-agent adversarial audit (`arc-llm-tooluse-mcp-not-done-before-audit`, 2026-06-28) found: **GENUINELY UNTRIED in-repo** — ripgrep for `tools=`/`tool_choice`/`function_calling`/`bind_tools`/ReAct across `python/carnot/agentic/` is EMPTY; the live LLM is a STATELESS one-shot proposer (`LocalGGUFProposer.induce`/`complete_text` → a single raw `/completion` POST, no tool schema) fired ~once per game on stall, orchestrated by the fixed Python `E3AgentPolicy` pipeline (EXPLORE→INDUCE→`plan_in_model` pure-Python BFS→verify→execute); the BFS/env/TRM are never exposed to the LLM as callable tools; TRM is retired+absent; the existing `python/carnot/mcp/server.py` is the INVERSE wiring (10 verify/repair tools for EXTERNAL clients to call Carnot's verifier — zero ARC tools, not on the ARC path). Closest precedents are DISTINCT: the verify→refactor re-induction loop (`arc_llm_reinduction.py:631`, ≤3 rounds) is a PYTHON for-loop injecting verifier counterexamples into the next one-shot prompt (context-injection, not LLM tool-driving), and the IGE cell-selector is an off-by-default passive ranker (nulled `no_first_win_lift_0.000`). **BUT — adversarially REFUTED on "would it plausibly beat the nulled context-injection":** the binding wall (`WALL_IS_HIDDEN_STATE`, exp4914) is information-theoretic, not lever-shaped — an LLM-with-tools only ever observes frame features + its own action sequence, the two input classes already proven insufficient (exp4914 order-state `observable=False`; exp4893 action-history null, `REPRESENTATION_INVARIANT_HARD` on held-out). Acting more just generates more of the same observable experience; it cannot manufacture an absent gradient. Compounding cons: the offline-legal scored agent must be the weak local 9B (even a 35B writes buggy one-shot world-models; a harder multi-turn tool-loop on a 9B is less reliable); RHAE = `min(human/agent,1)²` squares any extra ENV-interrogation actions (75% loss at 2× human); 8h/10-steps-sec cap makes a per-action tool-loop infeasible (only per-game/on-stall cadence is viable). **Honest prior it beats context-injection on live first-win ≈ 12%** — a touch above context-injection's null because it attacks a structurally-different axis (GENERATING new interaction-history vs RE-RANKING sampled experience), and because the SOTA ARC-AGI-3 winner (Executable World Models, arXiv:2605.05138, GPT-5.5 15/25) IS exactly this agentic tool-loop shape — but bounded hard by the hidden-state diagnosis + weak legal substrate + squared-RHAE. **Cheapest-decisive probe (if pursued): one OFFLINE dev-side A/B** — give a FRONTIER dev model (codex; offline-illegal for SCORING but legal for a DEV probe) a minimal tool schema over the EXISTING internal subsystems (`env.step`, `plan_in_model` expand/inspect, `WorldModelVerifier.score`, read+exec the induced `world_model.py`), bounded ~20 tool-turns, ZERO extra env GameActions (interrogate only internal/offline subsystems so RHAE is untouched), falsifiable gate = produces a first-contact L1 win on a truly-held-out unsolved game (e.g. re86) that the current one-shot induce+BFS pipeline does NOT. If a FRONTIER model with full tool access can't beat the one-shot pipeline at first-contact, the local 9B certainly can't → retire before any 9B/Kaggle scale-up. This decouples "does the tool-loop FRAMING help" (frontier ceiling) from "is the 9B too weak." Safest positive-EV use of the idea regardless: a frontier agentic tool-loop as a DEV/outer-loop convenience to write `GameAdapter` deltas faster (not the scored agent). Detail: `arc-generation-program-2026-06-28.md` (the wall), workflow `arc-llm-tooluse-mcp-not-done-before-audit`.
+
